  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: questions with do/does (review)",
      "title_form": "Preguntas con do/does en presente simple",
      "title_target": "Questions with do/does in present simple",
      "description_md_form": "Para preguntar sobre precios y compras en presente simple, usamos **do** o **does** al inicio de la pregunta.\n\n- Usamos **do** con *I, you, we, they*.\n- Usamos **does** con *he, she, it*.\n\nLa estructura es: **Do/Does + sujeto + verbo + ...?**\n\nEjemplos:\n- **Do** you pay with cash?\n- **Does** this store sell that item?\n\n**Importante:** cuando usamos **does**, el verbo principal va en su forma base, sin *-s*. Decimos *Does it cost...?*, no *Does it costs...?*.\n\nPara preguntar por el precio, usamos la estructura fija **How much does it cost?** (¿Cuánto cuesta?). Esta pregunta ya incluye *does*, así que no la cambiamos.",
      "description_md_target": "To ask about prices and shopping in present simple, we use **do** or **does** at the start of the question.\n\n- We use **do** with *I, you, we, they*.\n- We use **does** with *he, she, it*.\n\nThe structure is: **Do/Does + subject + verb + ...?**\n\nExamples:\n- **Do** you pay with cash?\n- **Does** this store sell that item?\n\n**Important:** when we use **does**, the main verb goes in its base form, without *-s*. We say *Does it cost...?*, not *Does it costs...?*.\n\nTo ask about the price, we use the fixed structure **How much does it cost?**. This question already includes *does*, so we do not change it.",
      "grammar_structure": "Do/Does + subject + base verb + ...?",
      "conjugation_table": {
